1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,231
A green pipeline does not always mean the original problem was fixed

2
00:00:04,231 --> 00:00:07,528
FaultLine C I checks the repair as well as the result

3
00:00:07,528 --> 00:00:11,510
This is a local evidence walkthrough with real Git and test runs

4
00:00:11,510 --> 00:00:13,999
The repair is scripted; Duo has not run.

5
00:00:13,999 --> 00:00:16,254
First, establish a healthy baseline

6
00:00:16,254 --> 00:00:20,957
The sample invoice calculator uses integer cents and percentage discounts

7
00:00:20,957 --> 00:00:22,697
All eight sample tests pass

8
00:00:22,697 --> 00:00:27,980
This exact local commit and the test results are preserved in the evidence bundle.

9
00:00:27,980 --> 00:00:30,551
Next, inject a one character regression

10
00:00:30,551 --> 00:00:33,387
The discount is added instead of subtracted

11
00:00:33,387 --> 00:00:37,277
Three pricing assertions now fail and five tests still pass

12
00:00:37,277 --> 00:00:41,827
These are measured local results, not hosted GitLab pipeline results.

13
00:00:41,827 --> 00:00:44,064
A scripted restoration fixes the sign

14
00:00:44,064 --> 00:00:45,637
All eight tests pass again

15
00:00:45,637 --> 00:00:53,801
The independent guard accepts the correction after checking commit ancestry, allowed change scope and the pinned pricing implementation

16
00:00:53,801 --> 00:00:56,220
This does not demonstrate an A I repair.

17
00:00:56,220 --> 00:00:57,566
Now the counterexample

18
00:00:57,566 --> 00:01:00,685
A different attempt disables the pricing assertions

19
00:01:00,685 --> 00:01:07,413
The tests report green, but the guard rejects the change: the tests were altered and the pricing fault remains

20
00:01:07,413 --> 00:01:10,961
This is why checking only pipeline status is insufficient.

21
00:01:10,961 --> 00:01:16,115
The repository includes the full reports, four J Unit files and a cloneable Git bundle

22
00:01:16,115 --> 00:01:20,010
Reviewers can inspect the exact commits and reproduce the command

23
00:01:20,010 --> 00:01:23,605
The local history is separate from the hosted merge request.

24
00:01:23,605 --> 00:01:27,444
The GitLab adapter and native repair instructions are implemented

25
00:01:27,444 --> 00:01:31,106
Account verification currently blocks both hosted jobs and Duo

26
00:01:31,106 --> 00:01:37,071
The next step is a real Duo proposal, human review and a green rerun checked through the GitLab A P I

27
00:01:37,071 --> 00:01:39,315
That live recovery remains unverified.
